      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "INFERENCE",
      "narration_text": "One answer is tiny. Google says a median Gemini text prompt uses 0.24 watt-hours, less than nine seconds of TV. That's Google's own figure, and images, video, and long reasoning cost more.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "LessonExcerpt",
          "props": {
            "header": "One text prompt",
            "subheader": "· Gemini, median",
            "rows": [
              {
                "tag": "ENERGY",
                "text": "0.24 Wh · under 9 seconds of TV",
                "emphasis": true
              },
              {
                "tag": "CARBON",
                "text": "about 0.03 g CO₂e"
              },
              {
                "tag": "WATER",
                "text": "0.26 mL · about five drops"
              }
            ],
            "footer": "Google's own figures (Aug 2025) · images, video, reasoning cost more",
            "sparkLine": "Tiny, one at a time."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-11-07T22:50:43.352733+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "actual_duration_s": 14.42,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "SCALE",
      "narration_text": "The catch is scale: billions of prompts a day. Data centres used about 415 terawatt-hours in 2024, one and a half percent of world electricity. The IEA projects 945 by 2030, driven mainly by AI.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "EvidenceBars",
          "props": {
            "title": "Data-centre electricity (TWh)",
            "note": "2024 ≈ 1.5% of world electricity",
            "bars": [
              {
                "label": "2024",
                "value": 415,
                "display": "415"
              },
              {
                "label": "2030 (projected)",
                "value": 945,
                "display": "945"
              }
            ],
            "accentIndex": 1,
            "caption": "All data centres, not only AI · IEA, 2025",
            "sparkLine": "More than double by 2030."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-11-07T22:51:47.640047+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "actual_duration_s": 17.51,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "CUT IT",
      "narration_text": "How to cut it: use smaller or distilled models, store their numbers with fewer bits, run on chips and data centres built for efficiency, when the grid is greenest. And don't use the biggest model when a small one will do.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "LessonExcerpt",
          "props": {
            "header": "How to cut it",
            "subheader": "· general techniques",
            "rows": [
              {
                "tag": "SMALLER",
                "text": "small or distilled models when good enough",
                "emphasis": true
              },
              {
                "tag": "FEWER BITS",
                "text": "quantization: less maths and memory"
              },
              {
                "tag": "HARDWARE",
                "text": "AI chips and efficient data centres"
              },
              {
                "tag": "CLEANER",
                "text": "run where and when the grid is greenest"
              }
            ],
            "footer": "Not every task needs the biggest model",
            "sparkLine": "Right-size the model."
          },
          "rendered": {
